.TH CEDIT 1 "November 2026" "cedit 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cedit \- lightweight Emacs-inspired terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cedit
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fB+\fILINE\fR[\fB:\fICOL\fR]] [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cedit
is a full-screen terminal text editor with Emacs-style key sequences,
UTF-8 support, syntax highlighting, multiple buffers, undo/redo,
incremental and regular-expression search, and atomic file saving.
Files that do not exist are created when first saved.
.PP
"GNU Cedit" is a working name; this program is not an official GNU
package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-emacs
Use the Emacs keymap (C-x C-s save, C-x C-c quit, ...).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-simple
Use the simple keymap (Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+Q quit, Ctrl+Z undo, ...).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-config
Do not read the configuration file or load any Lua scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Do not load scripts from the plugins directory.
.TP
.BI + LINE [: COL ]
Place the cursor at \fILINE\fR (and \fICOL\fR) in the next file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and whether Lua scripting is compiled in.
.SH KEYS
The default keymap follows GNU nano. ^X means Control-X; M-X means Alt-X
(or Escape followed by X). \fB^G\fR lists every active binding.
.TP
.B ^O\fR, \fB^S
Save.
.TP
.B ^X
Exit, offering to save modified buffers.
.TP
.B ^R
Open a file in a new buffer (TAB completes).
.TP
.B ^W\fR, \fB^Q\fR, \fBM-W\fR, \fBM-Q
Search forward, backward; next, previous match.
.TP
.B ^\e\fR, \fBM-R
Replace.
.TP
.B ^K\fR, \fBM-6\fR, \fB^U
Cut line or selection (repeat to append), copy, paste (\fB^U\fR).
.TP
.B ^6\fR, \fBM-A
Set mark. Shift+movement also selects.
.TP
.B M-U\fR, \fBM-E
Undo, redo.
.TP
.B ^_\fR, \fBM-G
Go to line[:column].
.TP
.B ^C
Show cursor position. In prompts, cancel.
.TP
.B M-\e\fR, \fBM-/
First, last line.
.TP
.B M-<\fR, \fBM->
Previous, next buffer.
.TP
.B ^]\fR, \fBM-.\fR, \fBM-,\fR, \fBM-H
Language server: complete, go to definition, go back, hover.
.TP
.B M-T
File tree sidebar: show and focus it; again, hide it. In the tree,
arrows move and fold, Enter opens, Esc returns to the text, q hides.
.TP
.B ^T
Run a command by name.
.PP
With \fB\-\-emacs\fR: C-x C-s save, C-x C-c quit, C-x C-f open, C-g
cancel, C-s/C-r search, C-k/C-y kill/yank, C-SPC mark, C-_ undo, M-x
commands, M-/ completion. With \fB\-\-simple\fR: Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Q,
Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Z/Y, Ctrl+X/C/V, Ctrl+F, Ctrl+P.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cedit/config
Configuration file (see \fBCONFIGURATION\fR). Honors \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cedit/init.lua\fR, \fI~/.config/cedit/plugins/*.lua
Lua scripts (only in builds with Lua). They must be owned by the user
and not group- or world-writable. Scripts are \fBnot sandboxed\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/cedit/recent
Recent-file history. Honors \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME\fR.
.TP
.IB FILE .save
Emergency copy written when the editor is terminated by a signal or runs
out of memory with unsaved changes.
.SH CONFIGURATION
One directive per line; \fB#\fR starts a comment line.
.PP
.nf
keymap nano|emacs|simple
tab-width 1-16
expand-tabs yes|no
auto-indent yes|no
auto-pair yes|no
mouse yes|no
lsp on|off
lsp LANG off
lsp LANG COMMAND [ARGS...]
line-numbers off|absolute|relative
theme dark|light|mono
colors auto|16|256|truecolor
face SLOT FG [BG] [bold] [italic] [underline] [reverse]
bind KEY... COMMAND
unbind KEY...
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Files are saved by writing a temporary file in the same directory,
syncing it to disk and renaming it over the original, so a failed save
never truncates the existing file. Permissions are preserved and
symbolic links are followed. Files with multiple hard links or owned by
another user are rewritten in place. Control characters and escape
sequences in files and filenames are displayed as visible text and never
sent to the terminal.
.SH LANGUAGE SERVERS
When a file is opened, the matching language server (clangd,
rust-analyzer, gopls, pylsp, bash-language-server,
typescript-language-server, vscode-json-language-server, taplo, marksman)
is started if it is installed. Servers are run without a shell. Some
servers execute project code (rust-analyzer runs build scripts); use
\fBlsp off\fR before opening untrusted projects.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit; 1 on startup errors; 2 on invalid options; 128+N when
terminated by signal N.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emacs (1),
.BR nano (1),
.BR vim (1)
.PP
Full documentation: README.md and docs/ in the source distribution.
